---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CTABand from '../../components/CTABand.astro';
import { photos } from '../../config/images';
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Current Sky', href: '/current-sky/' },
  { label: 'The Sky in 2026', href: '/current-sky/the-sky-in-2026/' },
];

const shifts = [
  { date: 'January 26', shift: 'Neptune enters Aries', note: 'from Pisces, where it had been since 2011', until: '2039' },
  { date: 'February 13', shift: 'Saturn enters Aries', note: 'from Pisces, since 2023', until: '2028' },
  { date: 'February 20', shift: 'Saturn conjunct Neptune at 0° Aries', note: '', until: '' },
  { date: 'April 25', shift: 'Uranus enters Gemini', note: 'from Taurus, since 2018', until: '2033' },
  { date: 'June 19', shift: 'Chiron enters Taurus', note: 'dancing between Aries and Taurus from June 2026 through April 2027, when it settles into Taurus until May 2034', until: '' },
  { date: 'June 30', shift: 'Jupiter enters Leo', note: 'from Cancer', until: 'July 2027' },
  { date: 'July 26', shift: 'North Node enters Aquarius, South Node enters Leo', note: '', until: '2028' },
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Sky in 2026: major planetary shifts"
  description="A look at the major planetary sign changes and longer cycles of 2026, with verified dates, astrological context, and Mo Lumen's interpretation of the larger patterns."
  path="/current-sky/the-sky-in-2026/"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
  <section class="hero hero--split">
    <div class="container">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The bigger picture</p>
        <h1>The sky in 2026</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Several slow-moving planets changed signs within the same stretch of months in 2026, and
          the lunar nodes changed signs as well. The useful story is not that one dramatic thing
          must happen; it is that several long cycles are changing symbolic context at once.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img
        class="hero__img hero__img--portrait"
        src={photos.skyReal2.src}
        alt={photos.skyReal2.alt}
        width={photos.skyReal2.width}
        height={photos.skyReal2.height}
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose flow" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-7);">
        <p class="eyebrow">At a glance</p>
        <h2>Four threads I am watching across the year</h2>
        <p>
          These are collective themes to observe, not forecasts of what will happen to an individual.
          A slow transit becomes personal through the natal chart and the circumstances already being lived.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        <article class="card"><h3>Vision meeting structure</h3><p>Saturn and Neptune coming together at 0° Aries raises questions about what happens when an ideal has to take form.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Information changing shape</h3><p>Uranus entering Gemini brings communication, knowledge, technology, movement, and networks into a longer period of experimentation and disruption.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Visibility and participation</h3><p>Jupiter entering Leo brings growth and enlargement into conversation with creativity, authorship, visibility, and self-expression.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Individual and collective</h3><p>The lunar nodes moving to Aquarius and Leo shift the eclipse axis toward questions of individual leadership and independence, Leo's generosity, and Aquarius's humanitarian, inclusive perspective.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose flow" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-6);">
        <p class="eyebrow">The astronomical framework</p>
        <h2>The year's major shifts</h2>
        <p>
          I like to begin with the movement itself before rushing to interpretation. From there, I
          look at the symbolism of the planets, signs, and aspects together to consider what new
          emphasis or atmosphere may be developing in the collective.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        {shifts.map((item) => (
          <article class="card sky-shift">
            <p class="card__meta" style="margin: 0;">{item.date}</p>
            <h3 style="margin: 0;">{item.shift}</h3>
            {item.note && <p style="margin: 0;">{item.note}</p>}
            {item.until && <p class="card__meta" style="margin: 0;">Remains in this phase until {item.until}</p>}
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="card__meta" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
        Positions are astronomy; the interpretation below is astrology.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <h2>Saturn and Neptune together in Aries</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/explore/planets/saturn/">Saturn</a> and <a href="/explore/planets/neptune/">Neptune</a>
        carry very different symbolic meanings. Saturn is associated with structure, limits,
        responsibility, discipline, time, and form; Neptune with permeability, imagination, dreams,
        idealization, illusion, and dissolution. Their conjunction at 0° Aries places those
        contrasting ideas at the beginning of the zodiac.
      </p>
      <p>
        One question I keep returning to is: <em>what happens when an ideal has to take form?</em>
        Aries adds themes of initiation, assertion, and beginning. That gives us a field of tension
        to watch rather than one event or one answer: vision and structure, inspiration and
        consequence, the impulse to begin and the reality of what beginning requires.
      </p>

      <h2>Uranus into Gemini</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/explore/planets/uranus/">Uranus</a> moved into Gemini, a sign associated with
        information, language, movement, exchange, and the ways ideas travel. Uranus is commonly
        read through disruption, invention, liberation, and sudden change. Put those symbols
        together and questions about communication, knowledge, technology, learning, and networks
        naturally come into view.
      </p>
      <p>
        I would resist turning that into a single prediction about society or a person. A slow
        transit becomes personal through the natal chart: the house it occupies, the planets and
        points it contacts, and the life already being lived there.
      </p>

      <h2>Jupiter into Leo</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/explore/planets/jupiter/">Jupiter</a> changes signs much more quickly than the
        outer planets, spending roughly a year in each. In Leo, its symbolism of growth,
        enlargement, confidence, meaning, and possibility meets a sign associated with visibility,
        creativity, heart, authorship, and self-expression.
      </p>
      <p>
        Expansion is not automatically improvement, and visibility is not automatically fulfillment.
        What interests me more is where this combination creates room to participate more fully,
        take something seriously enough to offer it, or notice where confidence has become excess.
        The relevant house and natal contacts tell us where that question becomes personal.
      </p>

      <h2>The nodes to Leo–Aquarius</h2>
      <p>
        In late July the <a href="/explore/lunar-nodes/">lunar nodes</a> moved onto the Leo–Aquarius
        axis, shifting the signs involved in upcoming <a href="/explore/eclipses/">eclipse seasons</a>.
        I am more interested in the relationship between the qualities of the two signs. Leo brings
        warmth, generosity, creative expression, and personal leadership; Aquarius brings
        independence and a humanitarian, inclusive perspective that looks beyond the individual.
        This axis raises questions about how Leo's generosity and willingness to lead can contribute
        to something larger, and how a broader collective perspective can still make room for
        individual expression and difference.
      </p>

      <h2>What to do with all this</h2>
      <p>
        At the collective level, these movements give us themes to observe over time. At the
        personal level, they become more specific only when we place them against a natal chart.
        Which houses are involved? Are exact aspects being made? What else is active? And what is
        actually happening in the person's life?
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABand
    heading="Keep watching the pattern as it unfolds."
    body="The annual view shows the long threads. Current Sky follows the individual events and changing sequence as the year moves forward."
    buttonLabel="Read Current Sky"
    buttonHref="/current-sky/"
    secondaryLabel="Open the Sky Calendar"
    secondaryHref="/current-sky/calendar/"
  />
</BaseLayout>
